{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cfe77f003e65e3c77e855a8ea37afcab888b6eead4c9d253cf7714d666947aa1","digest":{"component_or_area":"gen_env_registry script and env-vars.md documentation","key_entities":["scripts/gen_env_registry.py","docs/env-vars.md","os.environ.get","os.environ.pop","os.environ.setdefault","REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","scripts/check_config_ownership.py","tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py","KEY_BEARING","UnrecognisedEnvironAccess"],"problem_keywords":["environment variable registry","documentation drift","silent omission","AST scanner","os.environ access patterns"],"propositions":["The generator recognizes only os.environ.get, os.environ[...] subscript, and os.getenv forms, leaving os.environ.pop and os.environ.setdefault invisible to the scanner and unregistered in the generated registry.","Changing an environment read from os.environ.get to os.environ.pop silently drops the key from docs/env-vars.md with no error signal, violating the stated invariant that new env-var reads cannot ship undocumented.","The generator's silent fallthrough on unrecognized os.environ access patterns must be replaced with fail-closed behavior that raises an exception and aborts the build.","The local make lint gate must include the generator's --check validation to catch staleness immediately rather than only in the full CI suite, ensuring local and CI verdicts agree."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787553176364956001,"uuid":"4f131fb5-6cc1-4349-b8bb-1e5dcc9c2b8c"}